Portability fixes for mo_yanxi_vulkan_wrapper, applied by build.mcpp.

Both are upstream bugs rather than xrgui's, and both should go to
Yuria-Shikibe/mo_yanxi_vulkan_wrapper; this file is what keeps the tree
buildable until they do.

1. stack_trace.cpp -- `import` hoisted out of `#if defined(__cpp_lib_stacktrace)`.
   mcpp's M1 scanner rejects an import inside a conditional preprocessor block,
   even an inactive one. Importing unconditionally is harmless: where the macro
   is absent the import is simply unused.

   NOT expressed as a `[scan_overrides]` declaration. That was tried, and mcpp's
   audit rejected it for two reasons at once -- an implementation unit also
   imports the module it belongs to, and whether meta_programming is imported at
   all depends on the macro, so no single fixed declaration is true on both MSVC
   and clang.

2. util/exception.ixx -- three exception types moved from `std::exception` to
   `std::runtime_error`.

   `std::exception(const char*)` is an MSVC extension; the standard type has no
   such constructor, so the file did not compile on clang or GCC at all. The
   three `what()` overrides went with it: they only forwarded to the base, and
   each was declared without `noexcept` over a `noexcept` base, which is itself
   ill-formed ("exception specification of overriding function is more lax").

   This also removes a real defect rather than only a portability one. The
   argument was `msg.data()` on a `std::string_view`, which is not guaranteed
   NUL-terminated -- so a view over part of a larger buffer produced a message
   that ran past its end. runtime_error takes a std::string and copies it.

diff --git a/src/vk_wrap/stack_trace.cpp b/src/vk_wrap/stack_trace.cpp
index 795c514..3ce7b5e 100644
--- a/src/vk_wrap/stack_trace.cpp
+++ b/src/vk_wrap/stack_trace.cpp
@@ -4,10 +4,14 @@ module;
 
 module mo_yanxi.stack_trace;
 
-#if defined(__cpp_lib_stacktrace)
-
+// Hoisted out of the #if below: mcpp's M1 scanner rejects an import inside a
+// conditional preprocessor block, even an inactive one. Unconditionally
+// importing it is harmless -- when __cpp_lib_stacktrace is absent the import is
+// simply unused.
 import mo_yanxi.meta_programming;
 
+#if defined(__cpp_lib_stacktrace)
+
 void mo_yanxi::print_stack_trace(std::ostream& ss, unsigned skip, const std::stacktrace& currentStacktrace){
 	std::println(ss, "Stack Trace: ");
 
